// ============================================================================
// hipaa_164_528.dl — §164.528: Accounting of disclosures of protected
//                    health information
// ============================================================================
// "(a)(1) An individual has a right to receive an accounting of disclosures
//  of protected health information made by a covered entity in the six
//  years prior to the date on which the accounting is requested... (c)(2)
//  The covered entity must provide the first accounting to an individual in
//  any 12 month period without charge. The covered entity may impose a
//  reasonable, cost-based fee for each subsequent request... within the 12
//  month period, provided that the covered entity informs the individual in
//  advance of the fee and provides the individual with an opportunity to
//  withdraw or modify the request..."
//
// Scope-matched to required_by_164_524 (hipaa_164_524.dl): this predicate answers "was THIS
// disclosure_attempted tuple -- the covered entity's disclosure of the
// accounting document itself to the individual -- an owed obligation the CE
// failed to fulfill?" It deliberately does NOT attempt to derive WHICH past
// disclosures belong on the accounting list (the §164.528(a)(1)(i)-(ix)
// exclusion categories: TPO, to-the-individual, incident-to-permitted-use,
// authorized, directory/notification, national security, correctional/law
// enforcement, limited-data-set, pre-compliance-date) -- that would require
// evaluating six years of disclosure history and reconstructing document
// content, out of scope for a live single-narrative decision system (same
// reasoning as why §164.524's fee/content depth is oracle-backed, not
// reconstructed). Both are oracles here for the same reason.
//
// Used by: §164.502(a)(2)(i) (required_by_164_502_a_2_i's OR-branch,
// hipaa_164_502.dl) and §164.508(a)(4)/§502(a)(5)(ii)(B)(2)(vi)'s sale-of-PHI
// exclusion list (hipaa_164_508.dl) -- both previously depended on this stub
// always being false, silently treating every accounting-of-disclosures
// response as an un-required, potentially-a-sale disclosure.

.decl required_by_164_528(DECL_ARGS)

// is_accounting_request: oracle -- individual (or personal representative)
// has requested an accounting of disclosures under §164.528(a)(1).
.decl is_accounting_request(p2: Principal, p1: Principal, q: Principal)

// accounting_request_fulfilled: oracle -- the covered entity provided the
// requested accounting.
.decl accounting_request_fulfilled(p2: Principal, p1: Principal, q: Principal)

required_by_164_528(ARGS) :-
    is_covered_entity(p1),
    (p2 = q ; is_personal_representative(p2, q)),
    is_phi(t),
    msg_contains(m, q, t),
    is_accounting_request(p2, p1, q),
    !accounting_request_fulfilled(p2, p1, q),
    known_purpose(u).

// §164.528(c)(2): fee violation -- mirrors §164.524(c)(4)'s
// charged_unreasonable_access_fee gap-fix (hipaa_164_524.dl): a request that
// WAS fulfilled (!accounting_request_fulfilled fails, primary rule above
// can never fire) but subject to an impermissible fee -- no advance notice
// and opportunity to withdraw/modify, or charged at all for the first
// accounting in a 12-month period -- is still a violation of the
// individual's §164.528 rights, and without a fee-specific predicate
// nothing else in the formalization could ever flag it.
.decl charged_impermissible_accounting_fee(p1: Principal, p2: Principal, q: Principal)

required_by_164_528(ARGS) :-
    is_covered_entity(p1),
    (p2 = q ; is_personal_representative(p2, q)),
    is_phi(t),
    msg_contains(m, q, t),
    is_accounting_request(p2, p1, q),
    charged_impermissible_accounting_fee(p1, p2, q),
    known_purpose(u).
